# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# QA railguards.
#
# The per-branch reports in .qa/reports/ are COMMITTED and must stay that way:
# CI treats an absent report as a warning and exit 0, so an ignored report is a
# gate that silently stops enforcing. Do not add .qa/ here.
#
# The legacy shared root path stays ignored so a stray local copy cannot be
# re-committed. That is not theoretical: #398 untracked this file on
# 2026-05-28 and #434 — a sitemap PR — re-added it three days later, and the
# line below made it look untracked for ten weeks. gitignore does not apply to
# files that are already tracked.
.qa_report.json

