# Scripts directory (working scripts) - EXCEPT the explicitly named ones below.
# MUST be `scripts/*`, not `scripts/`: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so with `scripts/` every `!scripts/...` line below was
# inert and new files were silently untracked. The already-tracked ones survived
# only because gitignore does not apply to files already in the index.
scripts/*
!scripts/pr_overlap_guard.py
!scripts/r2_pdf_uploader.py
# Sol cross-review base selection. The pre-push hook shells out to this, and
# the hook FALLS BACK SILENTLY to the old whole-branch base if it is missing —
# so an untracked copy here would revert the fix on every other clone while
# leaving the hook looking fixed. Tested by tests/test_sol_review_base.py.
!scripts/sol_review_base.sh
# Cross-reference resolution pre-task artifacts (permanent QA artifacts)
!scripts/xref_pretask_setup.py
!scripts/xref_detection_audit.py
# Precinct boundary health check (run before/after every boundary import)
!scripts/verify_precinct_boundaries.py
# Granny-flat review-state measurement — the read-only query behind the badge
# change (which states are DISTINGUISHABLE in stored rows, and the before/after
# for every existing report). Committed so the claims can cite a command.
!scripts/measure_granny_confidence_states.py
!scripts/measure_climate_reference_availability.py
# Read-only census behind the flood three-state change: how many stored
# reports served a 'not in a flood zone' that was never established.
!scripts/measure_flood_zone_unassessed.py
# Container startup: fetch the Tweed/Wollongong flood grids from R2.
# Untracked here means every container starts without them, which is the
# defect this script exists to end.
!scripts/download_tweed_wollongong_rasters.py
# The 2022 flood calibration runner. Committed so the number in
# docs/qa/flood-calibration-2022-result.md can be reproduced, seed and all.
!scripts/run_flood_calibration_2022.py
# Read-only sweep for tests that assert an absence produces a NEGATIVE
# verdict rather than an unknown one — the class that hid the flood defect.
!scripts/sweep_absence_negative_tests.py
# Falsifiability plant-restore harness + the doc-claim checker. Both are
# imported by tests and invoked from .githooks/pre-push, so an untracked copy
# breaks every fresh clone — which is exactly the trap this line block warns
# about four comments above.
!scripts/falsifiability.py
# The lot-area repair. Tracked because the run against production is only
# auditable if the exact statement that rewrote 2.5M rows is in the history,
# and because it is the documented rollback path for that run.
!scripts/fix_lot_area_mercator.py
!scripts/doc_claims.py
# Builds the cdc_lot_link table (certificates -> cadastral lots). The table is
# live in production, so the recipe that produced it has to be in the repo or
# nobody can reproduce, audit or re-run it — and it needs re-running, because
# the certificate feed adds rows daily. Also the only place the development_type
# double-encoding fix is written down.
!scripts/build_cdc_lot_link.py
# Pre-merge guard: refuses to merge a PR whose gates run never ran. A
# CONFLICTING PR gets no Actions run at all, and an empty check list reads
# as 'not finished yet'. CLAUDE.md's merge workflow invokes this by path, so
# an untracked copy makes that instruction a lie in every fresh clone.
!scripts/check_pr_gates.py
!scripts/baselines/
!scripts/r2_upload_pdfs.py
!scripts/r2_monitor.py
!scripts/legislation_monitor.py
